invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier admits zero for r and for s. A zero s has the
  inverse zero, so R is the point at infinity, and a zero r never equals
  an X the equation computed: every test passes. FIPS 186-4 6.4.2
  refuses both before any arithmetic, and the proof requires the verdict
  0 and no call into the wide files for a pair outside 1..n-1.

--- old
    return p256_scalar_zero_mask(a) == 0 && p256_scalar_reduced_mask(a) != 0;
--- new
    return p256_scalar_reduced_mask(a) != 0;
